quran[18]{c,v,t}:
  98,8,"Their reward with their Lord is the Gardens of Eternity, with rivers flowing beneath them, abiding in them forever and ever. Allah is pleased with them, and they are pleased with Him. All this is for him who fears his Lord."
  99,1,"When the earth is shaken with its terrible quake,"
  99,2,"and when the earth throws out (all) its burdens,"
  99,3,and when humans say: ‘What is happening to it?’
  99,4,"on that Day, it will relate (all) its chronicles,"
  99,5,because its Lord will have inspired it.
  99,6,"On that Day, people shall proceed in separate groups to be shown their deeds."
  99,7,"So, whoever does an atom’s weight of good will see it,"
  99,8,and whoever does an atom’s weight of evil will see it.
  100,1,"By the galloping (war) horses, breathing pantingly (on the battlefields),"
  100,2,"by the strikers, striking sparks of fire (on rocks with their hoofs),"
  100,3,"by the raiders, launching raids at dawn,"
  100,4,"raising thereby a trail of dust clouds,"
  100,5,"and penetrating the middle of the enemy ranks,"
  100,6,"indeed, humans are ungrateful to his Lord."
  100,7,"Surely, he (himself) is a witness to that."
  100,8,"Indeed, he is extreme in the love of wealth."
  100,9,"Does he not know when whatever is in the graves is turned over,"
